WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:04.400
- [Narrator] K-pop band SHINee
is about to perform live

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:07.429
for more than a hundred thousand fans.

00:00:07.429 --> 00:00:11.870
- [SHINee Members] (speaking Korean)

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:14.420
- [Narrator] But none of
them are here in person.

00:00:14.420 --> 00:00:17.010
So, fans have paid about $40 each

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.823
to watch the spectacle from home.

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.610
That's because during the pandemic,

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:26.810
K-pop is taking livestream
concerts to the next level

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.433
by blending real and
virtual worlds together.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:33.910
Globally, many artists have
been livestreaming performances

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:37.798
for free on platforms like
Fortnite or Instagram.

00:00:37.798 --> 00:00:39.831
- [SHINee Members] Hi, we are SHINee.

00:00:39.831 --> 00:00:42.646
- [Narrator] But K-pop bands
are convincing fans to pay,

00:00:42.646 --> 00:00:45.904
especially after global
revenue from concerts last year

00:00:45.904 --> 00:00:49.026
dropped by 70% when
coronavirus restrictions

00:00:49.026 --> 00:00:51.932
brought music tours to a halt.

00:00:51.932 --> 00:00:54.932
- (speaking Korean)

00:00:56.864 --> 00:00:58.940
- [Narrator] We went behind the scenes

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:00.313
of SHINee's online concert

00:01:00.313 --> 00:01:02.930
to see how these extravagant livestreams

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:06.333
can be a lucrative way to help
reboot the concert industry.

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:15.600
These online concerts
are called Beyond LIVE.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.370
The concept was launched by the
K-pop label SM Entertainment

00:01:19.370 --> 00:01:22.050
as the coronavirus swept
across the US and Europe

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:23.810
around April of last year.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:26.810
- (speaking Korean)

00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:36.730
- [Narrator] Kim Sung-Hak's
company, Dream Maker,

00:01:36.730 --> 00:01:39.800
creates stage designs using
immersive technologies

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.061
to enhance visual effects
in online concerts.

00:01:43.061 --> 00:01:45.630
He says the idea is to deliver a show

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.520
that will be impossible to pull off

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:49.570
at a live, offline concert.

00:01:50.486 --> 00:01:53.486
- (speaking Korean)

00:02:08.691 --> 00:02:11.691
- (speaking Korean)

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:20.450
- [Narrator] This is the
first Beyond LIVE performance

00:02:20.450 --> 00:02:23.603
for SHINee, and it's taken
them some time getting used to.

00:02:24.583 --> 00:02:27.583
- (speaking Korean)

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:37.040
- [Narrator] In the past
year, Dream Maker has produced

00:02:37.040 --> 00:02:39.800
11 livestream shows for other K-pop bands,

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.803
including Super M and Twice.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:44.930
Kim says his team tries to recreate

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:47.690
the feeling of togetherness,
and for some bands,

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:50.583
FaceTime is a new part of
the concert experience.

00:02:52.684 --> 00:02:55.684
- (speaking Korean)

00:03:03.653 --> 00:03:06.440
- The last time I saw
them in person was 2017

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:08.706
when they came for the
SHINee World V tour.

00:03:08.706 --> 00:03:11.630
So the most exciting thing
was just seeing them,

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:12.463
to be honest.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:15.600
- [Narrator] Jenny Plyler is a SHINee fan

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.037
who lives in the US.

00:03:17.037 --> 00:03:19.420
She says while she prefers
physically attending

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:22.523
a live concert, she's happy to
see her favorite band online

00:03:22.523 --> 00:03:24.940
if that's the only possible way.

00:03:24.940 --> 00:03:27.220
- Sometimes the concert just
doesn't come to your country

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.150
for whatever reason,

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:30.137
like their schedules don't line up.

00:03:30.137 --> 00:03:32.706
(music beats)

00:03:32.706 --> 00:03:35.350
- The unique thing that is differentiating

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:38.670
the K-pop movement in relation
to what others are doing.

00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:41.040
It's a fan first approach,
which is really good.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.202
I think it's a great approach for music.

00:03:43.202 --> 00:03:45.827
- Mike Schabel is a concert
industry analyst in the US

00:03:45.827 --> 00:03:48.280
and he says Western artists can learn

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:51.510
from K-pop's approach
to these online shows.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:54.950
- It's the art in helping the audience

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:57.330
feel like their contribution matters.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:58.670
You know, their cheering matters.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.310
They feel like they're part of an event.

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:03.731
And that creates this
great dynamic and value.

00:04:03.731 --> 00:04:06.715
- [SHINee Members] (speaking Korean)

00:04:06.715 --> 00:04:09.715
- (speaking Korean)

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.170
- [Narrator] Lee Sung-Su is the CEO

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:21.675
of K-pop label SM Entertainment.

00:04:21.675 --> 00:04:23.900
He says his company had been working

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:27.664
on this new kind of fan
experience since 2012,

00:04:27.664 --> 00:04:31.204
but the pandemic kicked it into high gear.

00:04:31.204 --> 00:04:34.204
- (speaking Korean)

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:47.300
- [Narrator] And this advanced concert

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.710
comes with new revenue opportunities

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:52.880
by selling cheaper tickets
to a larger audience.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:55.240
For example, SHINee's Beyond LIVE

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:58.766
is at least $20 cheaper
than its in-person concerts,

00:04:58.766 --> 00:05:02.720
but the show could fill the
stadium eight times over.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:05.620
Plus, Beyond LIVE sells
merch for the online events,

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:08.350
like a stand for your
smartphone to watch the show

00:05:08.350 --> 00:05:12.250
or a fan light that syncs in
real time during the concert.

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:14.410
Lee declined to disclose total profits

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:16.324
from SM's Beyond LIVE concerts,

00:05:16.324 --> 00:05:20.280
but said that the venture
has been economically viable.

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:22.870
Even the South Korean
government is taking a page

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:24.981
from K-pop's online concerts.

00:05:24.981 --> 00:05:29.020
In March, it announced plans
to spend 17 million dollars

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:31.012
to create a virtual concert space

00:05:31.012 --> 00:05:33.460
to help smaller entertainment agencies

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:37.063
and independent labels
reach audiences online.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:40.650
But going virtual doesn't mean

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:42.830
the pandemic isn't a concern.

00:05:42.830 --> 00:05:45.530
The band and staff have to
get their temperatures checks

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:48.530
and fill out a questionnaire
before the concert.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:50.023
And when the pandemic passes,

00:05:50.023 --> 00:05:52.834
the band says it's looking forward to:

00:05:52.834 --> 00:05:57.251
- [SHINee Members] (speaking Korean)

